Create morph_mcp/jsonrpc.py for Python 3.9: the JSON-RPC 2.0 framing layer of an MCP stdio server. Standard library only.
Provide exactly four public names:
  read_message(stream) -> dict or None  -- read ONE newline-delimited JSON object from a text stream; return None at EOF; skip blank lines.
  write_message(stream, message: dict) -> None  -- write ONE compact JSON object followed by a single newline, then flush.
  success(request_id, result: dict) -> dict  -- build {'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':request_id,'result':result}
  error(request_id, code: int, message: str) -> dict  -- build {'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':request_id,'error':{'code':code,'message':message}}
A response carries either 'result' or 'error', never both.
PROTOCOL CONTRACT (stdio MCP, JSON-RPC 2.0, one compact JSON object per line, newline-delimited):
  -> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"protocolVersion":"2024-11-05","capabilities":{},"clientInfo":{"name":"c","version":"1"}}}
  <- {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"2024-11-05","capabilities":{"tools":{}},"serverInfo":{"name":"morph","version":"<any string>"}}}
  -> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"notifications/initialized"}      (a notification: no id, NO response at all)
  -> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"tools/list","params":{}}
  <- {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"name":...,"description":...,"inputSchema":{"type":"object",...}}]}}
  -> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"deck_status","arguments":{}}}
  <- {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<the tool output>"}],"isError":false}}
  Unknown method -> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":N,"error":{"code":-32601,"message":"..."}}
  A tool that raises -> a result with "isError":true and the message in the text content (NOT a JSON-RPC error).
The server reads stdin until EOF and never writes anything but protocol messages to stdout.

