Create morph_mcp/server.py for Python 3.9: the MCP stdio server wiring together the framing layer and the tool layer that are already in your context. Standard library plus this project only.
Run as `python3 -m morph_mcp.server`: read newline-delimited JSON-RPC from stdin until EOF, dispatch, write replies to stdout. Handle initialize, notifications/initialized, tools/list, tools/call; answer any other method with error code -32601; a notification (no id) gets no reply at all. A tool that raises must come back as a result with isError true carrying the message, never as a transport error. Nothing but protocol messages may go to stdout -- send any diagnostics to stderr.
The deck root is the current working directory, overridable with the MORPH_ROOT environment variable.
